L000525	
L000526	\section{Reaction scheme with an explicit fuel component}\label{sec:fuel}
L000527	Detailed balance is broken by a fuel $\tilde{\delta}$ according to Eq.~\eqref{eq:r_2_pathway}. Breaking detailed balance in this fashion is equivalent to the combined effect of the two reactions:
L000528	\begin{equation}
L000529	    A\xrightleftharpoons{k_u}{} B\, ,\qquad A+F\xrightharpoonup{k_\text{f}}{} B\, ,
L000530	\end{equation}
L000531	where the former reaction obeys detailed balance of the rates while the latter breaks it. The reaction rates of the unfueled $(r_\text{u})$ and fueled reaction $(r_\text{f})$ are
L000532	\begin{align}
L000533	    r_\text{u} &= k_u\left[\exp{\frac{\mu_A}{k_BT}} - \exp{\frac{\mu_B}{k_BT}} \right], \label{eq:r_u}\\
L000534	    r_\text{f} &= k_\text{f}\exp{\frac{\mu_A+\mu_F}{k_BT}}\, , \label{eq:r_f}
L000535	\end{align}
L000536	such that $r_B = -r_A = r_\text{u}+r_\text{f}$. Performing the mapping between these rates and the coarse-grained rate studied (Eq. \eqref{eq:r}), we find
L000537	\begin{equation}
L000538	    \tilde{\delta} = \log{\left(1+\frac{k_\text{f}}{k_u}\exp{\frac{\mu_F}{k_BT}}\right)}, \label{eq:delta_muF}
L000539	\end{equation}
L000540	where $\mu_F$ is the chemical potential of the fuel. Solving for the reaction rate coefficient of the fueled reaction $k_\text{f}$, we find
L000541	\begin{equation}
L000542	    k_\text{f} = k_u\exp{-\frac{\mu_F}{k_BT}}\left(\exp{\frac{\tilde{\delta}}{k_BT}}-1\right), \label{eq:k_f}
L000543	\end{equation}
